  "interpretation": [
    "This analysis separates retrieval failure from candidate-aggregation failure.",
    "A covered target is considered retrieval-successful when at least one of its historical training tickets appears among the 20 retrieved neighbors.",
    "Retrieval failure means the true training-observed assignee has no retrieved historical evidence within the Top-20 set.",
    "Aggregation failure after retrieval means the true assignee was retrieved but the MOD-007 summed-similarity aggregation did not rank it first.",
    "This decomposition determines whether a subsequent experiment should primarily modify retrieval or assignee scoring.",
    "Unseen evaluation targets are excluded from this covered-target retrieval analysis because they have no corresponding training-period assignee evidence."
